es": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "North Dakota remains one of the most Republican states in the country, with a partisan lean of roughly eighteen points toward the GOP. The 2028 presidential contest there is an open race with no incumbent on the ballot, and no candidate-specific polling, fundraising figures, or expert ratings are available. The forecast therefore rests on the state's underlying partisan balance.\n\nRecent headlines offer little to change that picture; state political news has centered on urging Governor Burgum not to seek the presidency rather than on the general election itself. Absent an extraordinary national shift, Republicans begin with a large built-in advantage, and the wide uncertainty reflects the lack of polling rather than genuine competitiveness.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0273, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0558, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0549, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0572, "margin": -18.0}]}